  "isWeedLegalHere": {
    "overview": [
      {
        "_key": "271f436a48a4",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "d4c7ba273ad20",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "In Dominica, the legal status of marijuana and related products is complex. While Dominica has decriminalized the possession of small amounts of cannabis for personal use, the country has not fully legalized the substance."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "885432a08bd5",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "9f93ee7eb4060",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Regarding specific cannabinoids, the situation is as follows:"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "186ecf4b294e",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cc8cfab9bb3f0",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "CBD: CBD is generally legal in Dominica, as long as it is derived from hemp containing less than 0.3% THC."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "609de828c371",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "2e72fe8c65200",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Delta-8 THC, Delta-9 THC, and THCA: These cannabinoids are considered illegal in Dominica, as they are derived from the cannabis plant and contain psychoactive properties. The possession, sale, or use of products containing these compounds can result in legal consequences."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5935227e3a17",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "8934c754d2000",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "In summary, while Dominica has taken steps to decriminalize personal cannabis use, the country maintains strict regulations on the production, sale, and distribution of marijuana and related products, including delta-8, delta-9, THCA, and CBD. The legal landscape continues to evolve, and individuals are advised to stay informed about the latest developments in Dominica's cannabis laws."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      }
    ],
