                "_key": "c0bff116d0880",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "In 2020, the government of Dominica passed an amendment to the Drugs (Prevention of Misuse) Act, which decriminalized the possession of up to 28 grams (1 ounce) of cannabis for adults. However, the cultivation, sale, and possession of cannabis for recreational purposes remain illegal. The government has also indicated plans to establish a legal cannabis industry for medical and wellness purposes in 2023."
